.TH OMX-PANEL 1 "2026-10-26" "omx-panel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-panel \- check a skin package for an OpenMixer plugin panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-panel
.B \-\-version
.br
.B omx-panel
.B validate
.IR "skin.json | skin-package-directory" ...
.br
.B omx-panel
.B describe
.B \-\-descriptor
.I file
.RB [ \-\-panel
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-skin
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-remote
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-pages
.RB [ \-\-per\-page
.IR N ]
.RB "| " \-\-layout ]
.br
.B omx-panel
.B describe
.B \-\-stored
.I answer.json
.B \-\-format
.BR lv2 | clap
.RB [ \-\-skin
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-remote
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-pages
.RB [ \-\-per\-page
.IR N ]]
.br
.B omx-panel
.B describe
.B \-\-plugin
.I target
.RB [ \-\-descriptor
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-sha256
.IR hex ]
.B \-\-store
.br
.B omx-panel
.B vocabulary
.RI [ package / name ]...
.br
.B omx-panel
.B descriptors
.B \-\-installed
.br
.B omx-panel
.B picture
.B \-\-descriptor
.I file
.RB [ \-\-panel
.IR file ]
.B \-\-png
.I out.png
.RB [ \-\-stem
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-scale
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-style
.IR style ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omx-panel describe
prints the panel description of a descriptor and its refusals as JSON; with
.B \-\-pages
only the pages, the Easy controls first, cut at
.I N
slots (eight when left out) by the one cut every surface uses, the skin applied first and a
.B \-\-remote
file's declared pages, as given, replacing the derived ones; with
.B \-\-layout
the layout the description was derived from, the family's displays included, which is what the panel renderer draws.
.PP
.B omx-panel describe \-\-stored
.I answer.json
prints the same output cut from a descriptions-store entry instead of a descriptor:
.I answer.json
is what
.B omx-panel-store get \-\-json
printed for a key of the
.B \-\-format
given, and the skin, the remote pages and the pages are applied to it as above, so a derived entry prints what
.B describe \-\-descriptor
prints and an edited one prints the edit. It reads no descriptor:
.BR \-\-descriptor ,
.BR \-\-panel ,
.BR \-\-ns ,
.B \-\-plugin
and
.B \-\-layout
beside it are usage errors (an entry holds no layout, so a drawn view is still derived from the descriptor). A refused
entry prints its code and its sentence and exits 1.
.PP
.B omx-panel describe \-\-plugin
.I target
.B \-\-store
prints one plugin's entry in the descriptions store, as
.B omx-panel-store get
answers it.
.I target
is
.BI lv2: uri
or
.BI clap: path # id\fR.
The store is asked first, by the binary's SHA-256 (or
.BR \-\-sha256 )
and the plugin's source as installed; an entry any layer holds is printed and nothing is written. Otherwise the
descriptor (the one given, else the installed declaration, else the newest in DESCRIPTOR_DIRS, else one
.B plugin-hostd-probe describe
makes) is described with the port groups the LV2 complement infers for that plugin, and the entry is written to the
layer of the effective uid (the system layer as root, the user layer otherwise) and printed. One plugin, never a scan.
LV2_PATH is the LV2 search list (else /usr/lib64/lv2:/usr/lib/lv2:/usr/local/lib/lv2).
.PP
.B omx-panel validate
reads each skin given, a
.I skin.json
file or a directory holding one, and checks it against the skin package schema shipped with the package. Each skin prints one line: its path and whether it is valid, with the first problem found when it is not.
.PP
.B omx-panel vocabulary
reads each installed source a panel is laid out by and prints one line for each, where it was read from:
the contract directories, omx-contract's meanings, its standard units and the units the param-contract extension serves,
and the descriptor of each
.IR package / name
given. A line starts with
.B ok
or, for a source that is not installed,
.BR FAIL .
.PP
.B omx-panel descriptors \-\-installed
prints the path of each installed plugin descriptor, one per line, found under every contract directory
whatever contract major is installed.
.PP
.B omx-panel picture
draws a plugin's panel from its descriptor and declared panel alone into a PNG: the layout
.B describe \-\-layout
derives, every control at its declared default with the text its face writes, drawn by
.BR omx-panel-render .
The same files draw the same bytes; a declaration that changes what is drawn changes the picture. It prints the
picture's width and height. The renderer is
.BR OMX_PANEL_RENDER ,
else the one on the path; the look is the package's, in its default style unless
.B \-\-style
names another of its styles.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
every skin is valid; every source is read
.TP
.B 1
at least one skin is not valid; a source is not installed
.TP
.B 2
usage error, or a file could not be read
.TP
.B 3
.B modgui
has nothing to draw: the descriptor has no visible control (a synth whose parameters are not LV2 ports). Not a fault; a sweep records a skip.
.br
.B complement \-\-check
found a bundle of its own stale or out of date (see
.BR omx-complement-sync (1)).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMX_PANEL_RENDER
the
.B omx-panel-render
command
.B picture
runs
.TP
.B OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
a
.B :
list of contract directories, read in place of the installed one; the first that holds a package is the one read
.TP
.B OMX_CONTRACT_SCHEMA
an omx-contract.schema.json read in place of the installed one
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx-panel/schema/skin-package.schema.json
the schema a skin is checked against
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx-contract/contract.d
the contract directory, where no
.B OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
is set and pkg-config has no omx-contract (omx-contract-data installs it; omx-contract-devel adds the pkg-config file)
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx-contract/omx-contract.schema.json
the meanings a descriptor's controls play
.SH SEE ALSO
The skin package format, the panel description and the MOD GUI generator are documented in
.IR /usr/share/doc/omx-panel/ .
